<!-- Indonesian. The folder is values-in, not values-id: Java maps the ISO 639-1 code "id" to the
     legacy code "in", and Android resolves the resources by that legacy code. The platform itself
     ships its Indonesian strings in values-in on every API level, and aapt2 keeps values-id and
     values-in apart instead of normalizing them, so values-id would simply never be resolved.
     The language tag stays "id" in locales_config.xml and in APP_LANGUAGES. -->
